From b62bb40eadb202874bac7f6ce587fe28549d976b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:04:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: check the Dolby Vision output
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

System > Submit Log > "Check the Dolby Vision output" measures whether the
graphics card passes the bytes of the Dolby Vision transport through its
display pipe unchanged, with the card's own CRC of what leaves it
(hades-output-check of hades-diag, whose sources say how). The measure
needs the display for itself, so it is never made while Kodi runs:

- the button asks the tool first, with --probe and outside the environment
  of Kodi, whether the check can be made here. Where it cannot (an NVIDIA
  card, whose driver offers no CRC; no output with the tunnel, as on
  Polaris and Vega without amdgpu.dvbridge_dce=1; no TV connected; a driver
  without the CRC), it says why in a window and nothing else happens;
- where it can, it asks once, with "no" as the answer that a dialog closed
  by something else gives, and says that Kodi closes for about twenty
  seconds and that the TV may show a black or noisy picture in Dolby Vision
  meanwhile. On "yes" it writes the request into
  /storage/.cache/hades-output-check and starts Kodi again;
  hades-output-check.service makes the check before Kodi starts;
- when Kodi is back, the report is shown once (a window of its own, in a
  thread, so that the service goes on starting): what it found and what
  that means, in the language of the interface, then the report of the tool
  in English. The button shows the last report again before it asks.

Nothing of it runs unless the button is pressed. The button is not shown on
a system without the tool.

Texts in English and the three Spanish ones (tú in Spain and Mexico, vos in
Argentina; "televisión" in Mexico), numbered from 33400 so that they meet
none of the other changes of this version.
